# Local config overrides (*.local pattern above covers vite.config.local.ts)

# tsc output from the .ts config files. Running tsc without --noEmit over this
# directory emits a .js/.d.ts beside each config source; they are untracked but
# not ignored, so they end up staged by a `git add -A`. Two reasons that hurts:
# Vite resolves vite.config.js *before* vite.config.ts, so a stale artifact
# silently shadows the real config, and vite.config.local.* is compiled from
# the private kindred-local symlink, so committing it would leak camp config.
# The inner * is load-bearing: it catches the .local and .local.example
# variants too, which `*.config.js` alone would miss.
*.config*.js
*.config*.d.ts
!eslint.config.js

# Test coverage output
coverage/